{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" motiv"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":"ic Galois groups should be a universal object that acts on all cohomology realizations of motives, preserv"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":"ing the polynomial relations among periods. The construction requires solving several deep problems: building a"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" proper category of mixed motives, establishing the standard conjectures for pure motives to form a Tannakian category, and proving the period conjecture that"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" connects the motivic Galois group to transcendence properties of periods. For tractable subcategories like Tate motives, the motiv"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":"ic Galois group is well-defined and relates to multiple zeta values, but for all motives over Q it remains conjectural. I'm thinking"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" about how to structure this exposition\u2014starting from classical Galois theory and the"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" Tannakian perspective, then moving through cohomology theories and periods, before building up to what"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" motives should be and why the Galois group matters."}}
