{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" -"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" Betti cohomology gives topological information when the variety"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" is defined over the complex numbers, de Rham uses algebraic differential forms, \u2113-adic \u00E9tale"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" cohomology works over any field, and crystalline cohomology handles positive characteristic. Each"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" satisfies the standard axioms for a Weil cohomology theory.\n\nOver the complex"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" numbers, Betti and de Rham cohomology are isomorphic after tensoring with C,"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" but the choice of rational bases on each side produces a matrix of complex numbers called the"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" periods. These appear in concrete examples like the 2\u03C0i from"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" the punctured line, the lattice generators of an elliptic curve, and special"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" values of zeta functions and polylogarithms - all mysterious transcendental numbers with deep arithmetic"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" meaning.\n\nGrothendieck envisioned a universal \"motivic\" cohomology theory that would explain why all these different approaches"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" give consistent results, with motives themselves constructed as"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" pieces of variety cohomology related through algebraic correspondences."}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":"\n\nIf"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" the category of motives forms a Tannakian category, it yields a motiv"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":"ic Galois group whose representations recover all the standard cohomology theories, and"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" the Galois group of the rationals should embed into it"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":". The period conjecture would then bound the dimension of this group by the transcendence degree of the periods themselves.\n\nThe main obstacles are"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" that constructing motives rigorously requires unproven standard conjectures, mixed"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" motives only exist in triangulated form so far, and the period conjecture vastly generalizes classical transc"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":"endence results - with specific cases connecting to multiple zeta values and Feynman integrals in"}}
{"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"thinking_delta","thinking":" physics."}}
